WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:35.131
This is Volcan. A screen reader reads a patch one plus sign at a time. Volcan turns it into sound, speech and Braille, with one key press. Listen.

2
00:00:35.131 --> 00:00:57.840
The earcon came first, so the verdict arrived before the sentence. This patch touches security, so the cue falls; a clean patch gets a rising cue. The sentence opens with the finding itself. The engine meter reads local heuristic, because this run has no cloud credentials, and the round trip was measured in this browser.

3
00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:22.489
Now a real pull request, read from GitHub without a token. Alt and 6 jumps to the address box, and Enter opens it. The page outlines the next steps; ask for the findings. Listen.

4
00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:58.993
Request changes stages the review, bound to the head commit Volcan read, under a single-use grant, and outlines Confirm. Nothing leaves until you say it. Confirm, and listen.

5
00:01:58.993 --> 00:02:16.640
Under the page is Volcan's Model Context Protocol server, written by hand to revision 2025-11-25. This button runs a real handshake: the negotiated version, a session identifier, and all twelve tools with their schemas.

6
00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:39.163
On this commit, 725 tests pass, and 23 of 23 protocol conformance checks. This button replays Amazon's documented Alexa+ requests as three clients; all three are served. Alexa+ itself has never called Volcan. Volcan: code review by ear and by touch.
